+\ variable with its compile-time default, so it has to run BEFORE the NVRAM
+\ store is read, never after. arch_init -- which calls nvconf_init() -- is
+\ registered from C as a PREPOST-initializer, and list-add APPENDS, so a
+\ PREPOST entry compiled into the dictionary here is reached first and the
+\ store's values land on top of the defaults, which is the intent.
+\
+\ As a SYSTEM-initializer (what x86, amd64 and ia64 all shipped) it runs in
+\ the NEXT list instead, i.e. AFTER nvconf_init has loaded the store -- so a
+\ perfectly good store was read, parsed, applied to /options, and then thrown
+\ away every boot. ppc/qemu, sparc32 and sparc64 -- the three arches anyone
+\ actually boots -- all say PREPOST-initializer here. The never-finished
+\ three copied the line into the wrong list.
 :noname
   set-defaults
-; SYSTEM-initializer
+; PREPOST-initializer
 
 \ preopen device nodes (and store the ihandles under /chosen)
 :noname
@@ -78,7 +91,31 @@ finish-device
 ; CONSOLE-IN-initializer
 
 \ Load VGA FCode driver blob
+\
+\ device-end FIRST, and it is load-bearing. Line 9 of this file executes
+\ `" /" find-device` and NOTHING closes it, so everything below runs with the
+\ ROOT NODE as the current device -- and `value` is $create, which defines into
+\ the CURRENT VOCABULARY. Without this, `vga-driver-fcode` lands in root's
+\ method list instead of the dictionary: measured on x86, `dev / words` prints
+\ it, a bare `$find` returns 0, and drivers/pci.c:1045's
+\ `feval("['] vga-driver-fcode 2 cells + 1 byte-load")` -- which runs with the
+\ PCI device node current, not root -- reported it undefined every boot.
+\
+\ The report is one token long and looks like progress: interpreter.fs:64 does
+\ `type 3a emit` (the word, then a colon) before throwing -13, and feval's
+\ caller prints no status, so the whole failure is the string
+\ "vga-driver-fcode:" with no newline. This lab had already written that string
+\ into drivers/floppy.c as a boot LANDMARK. The FCode driver has never been
+\ evaluated on x86 or amd64.
+\
+\ arch/ppc/ppc.fs carries the same block and never calls find-device, so ppc's
+\ copy is a global word and ppc's VGA has always worked -- which is why this
+\ survived: it is broken only on the arches nobody boots.
+\
+\ Same defect as patches 14 and 16 (bind_func before device_end), third
+\ instance, this time in Forth rather than C.
 [IFDEF] CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA
+  device-end
   -1 value vga-driver-fcode
   " QEMU,VGA.bin" $encode-file to vga-driver-fcode
 [THEN]
