+\ THE FIX IS NOT A PLUGGABLE ALLOCATOR. `alloc-tree` is called INSIDE
+\ encode-int, where the caller cannot reach it, so a "destination" it consulted
+\ would have to live in a variable -- a mode flag wearing a parameter's clothes,
+\ and a cached fact about which arena you are in is the bug class this lab keeps
+\ finding. It would also leave the device-tree path and the toolkit path sharing
+\ one mutable global.
